  "scope_method": "CPU is (delta utime+stime)/CLK_TCK divided by observed monotonic interval, 100%=one logical core. Role mean is total observed CPU / total process-interval exposure; p95 uses linear interpolation over observed per-process intervals. Navigation/fault scope uses goal_published to acquisition_finished and excludes CPU intervals crossing either boundary. Group CPU sums observed navigation and planning-worker percentages at each sample. Samples are 1 Hz, not peaks/WCET. RSS/VM are per-process snapshots; summed RSS double-counts shared memory. Windows bracketed by samples do not imply capture of subsecond work or missing first process intervals. UTC labels may be adjusted; all durations use monotonic time.",
